Design decisions (packet delegates these):
- Facets counts use MINUS-OWN-DIMENSION semantics; `has_evidence` keys are `with`/`without`. Zero-population
  (empty base) returns empty maps for all three dimensions (200, no error) — literal acceptance reading.
- `_apply_asset_filters` is the ONE shared filter path for `list_assets` and `asset_facets`; the facets
  `q` uses the same `ensure_asset_fts` + `sanitize_fts_query` call.
- FTS field list (from `app/services/fts.py` DDL): `asset_fts(asset_id UNINDEXED, display_name,
  household_id UNINDEXED)` — `MATCH` searches `display_name` only. The client-side `q` re-filter touched
  `item.name` (= `display_name`), the same field, so it was REMOVED.
- Client category filter removed: the pill now passes the raw `asset_type` to the server; keeping the client
  match would have dropped `asset_type='unknown'` rows (mapped to `Uncategorized` by `toProductCategory`),
  so removal is correctness, not just redundancy.
- Pills are `All (N)` plus one `key (N)` per real `asset_type` facet key; the `All` count is the sum of the
  `asset_type` facet map (= unfiltered-with-`q` total). No `AppShell.tsx` change was needed: pill labels are
  computed in `CatalogPage` and the existing `categories: readonly string[]` prop is reused.
- G3 fix: list serializer now sends `evidence_ids` (the field the card reads), not the full `evidence`
  records.

